# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Terraform state contains EVERY secret in plaintext — DB password, API keys,
# storage connection string. It must never reach source control.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
.terraform/
crash.log
crash.*.log

# NOTE: .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. Commit it — it pins
# provider versions so every engineer and the CI runner resolve identically.
# It is generated on first `terraform init`.

# Variable files holding real values
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
secrets.auto.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# Plan files embed variable values, including secrets
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*

# Service principal credentials
azure-credentials.json
sp-output.json

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
